<h2 id="five-stages-one-direction">Five stages, one direction</h2><p>Every idea on the ledger moves through the same five stages: Discover, Develop, Validate, Brief and Implement. The stages are not paperwork. Each one asks a different question, and an idea only moves on when that question has a good answer.</p>
<h2 id="what-each-stage-asks">What each stage asks</h2><p><b>Discover</b> asks whether the problem is real and who has it. <b>Develop</b> asks whether a working version can be built. <b>Validate</b> asks whether it works in the field, for whom and at what cost. <b>Brief</b> asks whether decision-makers can act on the evidence. <b>Implement</b> asks whether someone is willing to adopt it.</p>
<blockquote>A stage is finished when its question is answered, not when its time is up.</blockquote>
<h2 id="why-we-show-the-stage-in-public">Why we show the stage in public</h2><p>Every idea page and initiative shows its stage as a rail. Anyone can see where an idea stands and hold us to moving it forward honestly, including when an idea stops because the evidence says it should.</p><p class="tags"><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=method">#method</a><a class="tg" href="{{ route('insights.index') }}?tag=pipeline">#pipeline</a></p></article></div></section>
